speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, my hon. friend says that the government promised that prosperity would trickle down. That is a false statement. The government never said any such thing. If my hon. friend begins his question with an inaccurate statement, then one can only conclude that the rest of the question is also seriously flawed, as indeed it is.
How does one deal with poverty? By creating jobs;
48,000	last month. There were 1.4 million new jobs created since this government came into office, the highest job creation record of the G-7 countries. The government has done this by keeping inflation low. Inflation is now at a 30-year low at 1.5 per cent or thereabouts.
